implementationPlan.note:
New module context/contextPacket.ts (~140 lines with doc comments). It is pure. It exports:
- MANDATORY_SECTIONS (7 paths), plus the internal conditional task.requiredCheckSnapshot;
- the budget constants DEFAULT 100000, MIN 1000 and MAX 250000;
- readPacketBudgetChars: strict, refuses invalidInput('packetBudgetChars') and never clamps;
- the PacketSection, PacketManifest and PacketInput types (status = Extract<SourceItemStatus> from C02);
- buildPacketManifest.
Internally it has an own-property path reader, servable() and omissions().
Provenance ids are string|null: an odd shape gives null, never an invented id.
Snapshot run (removed afterwards): the builder unit test is GREEN, the status/no-task test passes (a regression guard), and the 17 get_context cases are RED for the right reasons: ROLE_OMITTED is not exported, packetManifest is undefined, and packetBudgetChars is accepted.

comments.content:
Dependency note, 2026-10-25, from the architect planning C02 on the operator's decision: C01 now also dependsOn C02 (task-b23c65b0), and C02 no longer depends on C01. C02 is planned and WORKING. It defines the repository-source vocabulary in packages/moe-daemon/src/context/repositorySource.ts:
- per-query SourceItem with status served|truncated|omitted|missing|refused|unavailable and exact reason codes;
- result-level complete flag;
- sorted limitation codes, e.g. committed-bytes-only, literal-search-only, repository-unavailable;
- manifest { commit };
- serveRepositorySource's taskId + planRevision.

When C01 unblocks, map the packet's "source provenance, limitations and explicit omissions" onto these landed types rather than defining a parallel scheme. Re-verify against the landed file first. C01's existing block (blockedOnTaskIds F03-F06) is unchanged.
